                <pb facs="0525" n="453" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg453"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6369/268.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Merry to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                            Jose</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-11-11"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">November 11,
                    1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Merry says that Nicaraguan Army while fighting revolutionists offensively
                    invaded Costa Rica on the southern bank of San Juan River, and that Costa Rica
                    had asked explanation from Managua.</p>
            </div>
